// Version and range behavior against test data from the npm `semver` package and the Rust `semver`
// crate that Cargo uses, plus hand-written rows for errors, overflow, and the pre-release options.
// The npm rows come from test/fixtures (range-include, range-exclude, the option-free table of
// range-parse, valid-versions, invalid-versions, comparisons, equality); rows that need `loose`
// mode, numbers above 2^53, or forms Silk rejects on purpose (a lone `+build` token, `vvv1`, a
// pre-release after a wildcard) are left out. The Cargo rows come from tests/test_version_req.rs
// and tests/test_version.rs of the crate.
//
// Each row is tab-separated. `npm`, `npm+`, and `cargo` rows give a range, a version, and `1`, `0`,
// or `E` (the range does not parse). `eq` rows give an npm range, the canonical form the `semver`
// package prints for it, and numbers: both must agree on every version made from those numbers.
// `ver` rows give a version and whether it parses; `cmp` rows give two versions and their
// precedence, and `ord` rows their total order with build metadata. `cargo+` and `npm+` rows use
// `matchesIncludingPrerelease`. `err` rows give a parser, a text, and the error reason and offset.
// `next` rows give a version and its next major, minor, and patch releases.
fn rows() -> [string<'static>; 867] {
